{
    "meta": {
        "purpose": "Player-shaped Magic card-search questions for eval. Mix of asks the live app can serve today and harder searches we want later. Not an exhaustive relevant-set; expected_cards are tripwire exemplars.",
        "use": "scripts/eval_retrieval.py and eval_judge.py score every row the same way: embed the raw query and run search_card_text. That is today's retrieval floor. Split scores by coverage — current is the live product, aspirational is the backlog.",
        "path": "Planner route: text_search, seed_card, or unsupported. Matches src/llm.py. Eval does not run the planner or the seed-card ability split.",
        "coverage": "current = one oracle-text vector query (or the live seed path) is enough. aspirational = needs more than MiniLM on a sentence.",
        "gap": "What a future planner — a thinking model that writes SQL — would have to add on top of a single embedding. filters: predicates on cards (color, mana value, type, keywords, legality); slang: expand ramp/burn/wipe/tutor into oracle wording; price: budget/cheaper (not in this database); negation: e.g. lands that do not enter tapped. Aspirational rows are deliberate future searches, not mislabeled current ones. gap is not consumed by retrieval yet; it is the spec for that SQL layer.",
        "sub_intent": "Older query-shape tags. Unused by eval."
    },
